                <pb facs="1146" n="1036" sameAs="frus:frus1931v03/pg1036"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51 Contractual Obligations/22: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-01-16T17:00:00+08:00">January 16, 1931—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received January 16—9:10 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>27. Department’s 3, January 3, 6 p.m. I have transmitted through the Foreign
                    Office a letter addressed to Dr. Wang Chung-hui, Chairman of the Commission for
                    the Reorganization of China’s Domestic and Foreign Loans, stating the
                    Department’s attitude as outlined in paragraph 4 of the above-cited
                    telegram.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
